  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39471314",
      "title": "Testing values",
      "lectureOrder": 458,
      "videoOrder": 421,
      "sourceHash": "f47a1be0c535ae4fd8d380d6a0053bf9c61bae1e4e0d4541903e9afdfcf93291",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.44,
          "end": 3.98,
          "en": "Let's now have a look at how we can test values in Bash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.04,
          "end": 9.68,
          "en": "And if we want to test values, we can and should use the double square brackets for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.71,
          "end": 10.79,
          "en": "Why do I say should?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.82,
          "end": 13.6,
          "en": "Because there are also other ways to test for values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.61,
          "end": 15.86,
          "en": "We will have a look at those later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.86,
          "end": 20.24,
          "en": "So you know that those are things that you might want to avoid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.24,
          "end": 22.58,
          "en": "And we will also have a look at the reasons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.58,
          "end": 24.5,
          "en": "But that's the reason why I said should.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.53,
          "end": 29.21,
          "en": "So if we want to test for values, we can use the double square brackets for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.21,
          "end": 34.94,
          "en": "And inside those, we can declare our condition that should be evaluated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.24,
          "end": 43.79,
          "en": "This test will then set the exit code to zero if the condition has been fulfilled and to one or to false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 43.79,
          "end": 46.16,
          "en": "when the condition has not been fulfilled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.86,
          "end": 50.25,
          "en": "So as a first example, let's say we have this condition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.25,
          "end": 50.67,
          "en": "Hello?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.67,
          "end": 52.05,
          "en": "Equals equals hello.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.05,
          "end": 54.93,
          "en": "And of course there this condition is fulfilled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.93,
          "end": 61.41,
          "en": "So of course here the result is true, meaning exit code of zero if we have a look at this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.62,
          "end": 62.55,
          "en": "So here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.55,
          "end": 63.21,
          "en": "Hello.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.21,
          "end": 65.22,
          "en": "Equals equals hello.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.22,
          "end": 67.65,
          "en": "And then double square bracket close.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.68,
          "end": 70.53,
          "en": "Then we can see here this has now executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.53,
          "end": 76.53,
          "en": "And if I now access the exit code of my previous command, we can see here it's now zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.95,
          "end": 79.11,
          "en": "Let's have a look at another example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.11,
          "end": 80.97,
          "en": "Hello equals equals world.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.97,
          "end": 83.76,
          "en": "And in this case, the condition is not fulfilled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.76,
          "end": 85.59,
          "en": "So the exit code will be one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.59,
          "end": 87.09,
          "en": "Let's have a look at this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.6,
          "end": 88.56,
          "en": "Hello.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.56,
          "end": 90.27,
          "en": "Equals equals world.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.08,
          "end": 93.06,
          "en": "And then double square bracket close.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.06,
          "end": 95.52000000000001,
          "en": "And we can see here, what's my exit code?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.52000000000001,
          "end": 97.53,
          "en": "We can see here it's one now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.28999999999999,
          "end": 102.25,
          "en": "The next thing is that we can also use different operands here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.25,
          "end": 105.37,
          "en": "So for example, we could also use an not equals here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.37,
          "end": 107.8,
          "en": "Hello, not equals word world.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.8,
          "end": 112.96000000000001,
          "en": "And then of course this condition is fulfilled and then the exit code will be zero again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.22999999999999,
          "end": 114.55,
          "en": "Let's have a look at this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.55,
          "end": 121.06,
          "en": "So here I just replace this with a exclamation sign and then the exit code is zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.06,
          "end": 129.22,
          "en": "Now, another thing is that those quotes here, they are not string quotes as usual in Bash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.22,
          "end": 132.25,
          "en": "So quotes here in Bash do not define a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.25,
          "end": 137.62,
          "en": "They just define which expansions should be applied there by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.62,
          "end": 139.81,
          "en": "Without those quotes it would work as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.81,
          "end": 142.3,
          "en": "Then just all expansions would be applied.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.39,
          "end": 145.99,
          "en": "But we want to disable quite a few of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.99,
          "end": 149.07999999999998,
          "en": "So that's why we are using double quotes here quite a lot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.07999999999998,
          "end": 153.73,
          "en": "And if we want to fill in a variable, we can of course also use variable expansion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.73,
          "end": 159.92000000000002,
          "en": "And then we could, for example, check whether a variable contains a certain value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.73,
          "end": 163.61,
          "en": "So let me create a variable here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.61,
          "end": 171.32,
          "en": "Let's call call the variable name and we just set it to yen and then I can try to access this variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 171.32,
          "end": 174.41,
          "en": "and compare it to max, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.41,
          "end": 177.98,
          "en": "And if I now output the exit code here, it's one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.98,
          "end": 180.59,
          "en": "So this condition has not been fulfilled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 181.79,
          "end": 184.16,
          "en": "I want to emphasize another thing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 184.16,
          "end": 187.31,
          "en": "I need a really simple example for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 187.67,
          "end": 188.51,
          "en": "Hello?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.51,
          "end": 189.62,
          "en": "Equals equals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.62,
          "end": 190.43,
          "en": "Hello.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.61,
          "end": 191.84,
          "en": "And this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.87,
          "end": 195.92,
          "en": "If I now output the exit code here, we can see here it's zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.13,
          "end": 201.56,
          "en": "I want to show you that here in this case, because it's only one word here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.19,
          "end": 205.13,
          "en": "We could also omit those double quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.16,
          "end": 208.37,
          "en": "We usually shouldn't, but it would also work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 208.37,
          "end": 210.68,
          "en": "And we can see here this is still the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.68,
          "end": 212.93,
          "en": "So those quotes really justified.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.93,
          "end": 215.42000000000002,
          "en": "Which expansions should be applied or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 217.07,
          "end": 218.32999999999998,
          "en": "This is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.32999999999998,
          "end": 225.49,
          "en": "For another thing, just as an example, what happens if I remove one of this whitespace here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 225.5,
          "end": 230.84,
          "en": "If I now execute this command, we can see here bash is indicating, Hey, continue typing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 230.84,
          "end": 232.04,
          "en": "I'm not done yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.19,
          "end": 233.66,
          "en": "Why is that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.69,
          "end": 237.61,
          "en": "Well, those double quotes here do not define a string in bash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 237.62,
          "end": 241.83,
          "en": "They only define which rules should be disabled within them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.58,
          "end": 246.69,
          "en": "And here in this case, this is the operand equals equals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 246.69,
          "end": 251.19,
          "en": "And all of this is considered to be the right side of our equals equals sign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 251.19,
          "end": 259.05,
          "en": "So it's comparing hello with this value here and the the double square brackets that we opened here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 259.05,
          "end": 261.84,
          "en": "Well, it's still waiting to close them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 261.84,
          "end": 262.62,
          "en": "To close them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 262.62,
          "end": 269.31,
          "en": "We need a whitespace so that we are outside of this right side operand of our equals equals sign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 269.31,
          "end": 275.64,
          "en": "And then we can close those double square brackets here at the beginning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 275.64,
          "end": 278.90999999999997,
          "en": "And now we can see now it could execute this command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 278.90999999999997,
          "end": 285.87,
          "en": "So here, this is extremely confusing, but this is considered part of this block here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 285.87,
          "end": 288.84000000000003,
          "en": "And this is being compared with this one here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 289.44,
          "end": 291.06,
          "en": "So just be aware of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 291.06,
          "end": 298.59000000000003,
          "en": "That whitespace, just one whitespace too much or too little can have an extreme influence on the way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 298.59000000000003,
          "end": 301.32,
          "en": "this command or this condition is being executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 301.32,
          "end": 309.09,
          "en": "And of course here in this case, this one is false because hello is not equal to hello with two square",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 309.09,
          "end": 310.26,
          "en": "brackets at the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 310.71,
          "end": 316.86,
          "en": "Another thing that I would like to mention is that there are also different expansion rules that are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 316.86,
          "end": 319.08,
          "en": "valid for the double square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 319.08,
          "end": 324.81,
          "en": "Block So, for example, word splitting and pathname expansions are disabled within them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 326.22,
          "end": 332.79,
          "en": "Other expansions such as variable expansions and command substitutions here are still working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 332.82,
          "end": 334.2,
          "en": "This is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 334.2,
          "end": 336,
          "en": "I want to show you an example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 336,
          "end": 343.74,
          "en": "So here, this would usually, if I would do this directly in Bash, it would expand to all the files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 343.74,
          "end": 350.49,
          "en": "that end with TXT in my current directory and then it would create this list and in this case it would",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 350.49,
          "end": 355.77,
          "en": "try to see if this is command that a command that can be executed better would be if I would write it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 355.77,
          "end": 356.4,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 356.4,
          "end": 363.48,
          "en": "And then we can see here Bash has now found all the dot txt files and they are now those file names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 363.48,
          "end": 369.87,
          "en": "have now became become arguments to our echo and they are now outputted this is disabled within this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 369.87,
          "end": 370.5,
          "en": "one here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 370.5,
          "end": 378.45,
          "en": "So if I would write something like this star dot txt equals equals star dot txt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 378.63,
          "end": 382.59,
          "en": "Then we can see here this is still zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 382.86,
          "end": 384.57,
          "en": "So this is still true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 384.57,
          "end": 392.58,
          "en": "Even though here I did not have any quotes around because here this pathname expansion has not been",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 392.58,
          "end": 395.7,
          "en": "applied because this is disabled by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 395.7,
          "end": 399.3,
          "en": "Within those also the word splitting is disabled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 399.3,
          "end": 405.12,
          "en": "This doesn't mean that, for example, this one equals to hello world.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 405.12,
          "end": 413.04,
          "en": "This still creates a syntax error because it doesn't know where the second the right side of this operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 413.04,
          "end": 413.46,
          "en": "ends.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 413.46,
          "end": 419.01,
          "en": "So we can see here there's still a syntax error here, but if this one here was within a variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 419.19,
          "end": 423.03,
          "en": "this variable would not be expanded into multiple words here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 423.45,
          "end": 429.69,
          "en": "So if here I would try to access a variable that would happen to contain Hello world that would then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 429.69,
          "end": 434.52,
          "en": "still be considered just one world, just one word instead of multiple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 434.52,
          "end": 441.03,
          "en": "It would not be split into multiple bash words or multiple arguments here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 441.42,
          "end": 446.67,
          "en": "If it comes from a variable, it will always be considered to be a single string and the string will",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 446.67,
          "end": 449.31,
          "en": "not be taken apart into multiple words.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 449.31,
          "end": 455.19,
          "en": "So that's what I meant here with word splitting is disabled within those double square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 456.36,
          "end": 458.73,
          "en": "We can, by the way, also see this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 458.76,
          "end": 463.83,
          "en": "If I would actually create this variable and write Hello World in it, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 465.51,
          "end": 466.35,
          "en": "Hello, world.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 466.35,
          "end": 467.01,
          "en": "And like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 467.04,
          "end": 469.26,
          "en": "Of course, now this variable exists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 469.26,
          "end": 473.01,
          "en": "And now I could try to execute this one here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 473.01,
          "end": 480.87,
          "en": "And we can see here this is now considered true because here this variable has been taken as one word,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 480.87,
          "end": 482.43,
          "en": "like one bash word.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 482.88,
          "end": 490.29,
          "en": "And this string has not been splitted into multiple words because we are within those double square",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 490.29,
          "end": 491.07,
          "en": "brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 491.46,
